.TH BEACON-STATUS 1 "August 2026" "beacond 1.4.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
beacon-status \- query a beacond instance's health endpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beacon-status
[\fB\-e\fR \fIendpoint\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beacon-status
queries a running
.BR beacond (8)
instance's
.B /health
endpoint with
.BR curl (1)
and prints the JSON response.
Exit status is 0 when the beacon answers, 1 otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-e " endpoint"
beacond base URL.
Default: the
.B BEACON_ENDPOINT
environment variable, or
.I http://127.0.0.1:9911
if that is unset.
.TP
.B \-h
Show a short usage message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BEACON_ENDPOINT
Default endpoint, normally set by
.IR /etc/profile.d/beacon-env.sh .
See
.I /usr/share/doc/beacond-client/README.Debian
for how to override it per host without editing that file directly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
beacond answered.
.TP
.B 1
beacond did not answer, or curl is not installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR beacond (8)
